Z||000000||DaRkLoRD||08-01-2000||04:55 AM||||After a month of trying different methods of printing, after replacing both print cartridges, re-aligning the print heads, adjusting the paper feed.. (and asking my printer very politely to please work...   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">)<BR>I realized it's not working as I'd planned.<P>I'm sorry it's taken so long, I had hoped to fix the printing problem myself, but I couldn't.. so instead of sending out cards that are printed slightly crooked (it's off by almost 1/4" near the top and bottom of the page!) I've decided to pay a little extra and get the cards professionally printed. They won't be as durable, but they should be fine.. in the tests I did, I had the cards totally soaked through.. and only after playing with the cards for a while did they start to come apart. They curl up when they get wet, but the ink does not run at all.<P>I'm sending in this order along with another order for a client, to save on shipping costs. there's a one week turnaround, so I should have the Fiero Project cards by the end of next week.<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fpcard-front.jpg">   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fpcard-back.jpg">  <P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A><p>[This message has been edited by DaRkLoRD (edited 08-01-2000).]||||reg||3
